{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789417453,"nonce":"i65fb8jan2FA/0d5CXc0SOhDdG8=","message":"Stage 3 landed (two threads run Wren on one heap; e2e\ntwo_threads_run_wren_on_one_heap: both load modules, define classes,\ncreate closures and generator fibers, tier up, print, and collect\nwhile the other runs; 700 plain and 40 stressed iterations clean).\n\nWhat it took, each found by a race the test hit:\n- MethodCache per view; the collector bumps a collection count and\n  a view that slept through one invalidates on resume.\n- CallSiteIC is a seqlock: kind carries a write count, the writer\n  zeroes it, writes the fields, publishes a fresh count; readers\n  copy and re-check. Compiled code never read IC memory at runtime\n  by default (Cranelift bakes the snapshot), so no codegen change.\n- Interner: chunked append-only storage reached through a fixed\n  table (resolve is lock-free, slots never move), RwLock on the\n  name map; serde wire shape unchanged so existing .hatch load.\n- Engine: tier_lock (a small reentrant lock in stw.rs) around\n  request_tier_up / poll / drain / native_tick / speculation /\n  threaded-code / bytecode lowering once threaded; compile results\n  install only with the world stopped (VM::install_compilations,\n  driven from safepoints when the broker flags results_ready, and\n  from collect_garbage while stopped).\n- Module install, meta compile/eval registration and\n  module_sources insert under stop_world (a StoppedWorld guard);\n  closure_fns pre-sized under the stop so a MakeClosure never grows\n  it. Output locked once threaded.\n- A fiber runs on the thread that made it (ObjFiber.thread).\n- After a collection on another thread, leave_safe drops live-regs\n  entries of fibers that were freed (the collector's forget_stack\n  only reaches its own thread's registry).\n- Bytecode lowering raced: two threads each installed an Arc and\n  dropped the other's under its reader — now under the tier lock.\n\nNot done, by design or yet: List/Map mutation from two threads is\nthe program's race (a Mutex class comes with stage 4); the\nembedder's handles and reload state are not locked; C-API entry\npoints do not mark the thread running/safe (interpret does).\nNUC numbers unchanged. Next: stage 4, the pool and Fiber.go.","files":null}]}